# Build-context excludes for Dockerfile.base ONLY (BuildKit uses <Dockerfile>.dockerignore when
# present, INSTEAD of .dockerignore -- so this must repeat the general excludes too).
#
# The critical extra vs .dockerignore: keep ALL team/reference agent code OUT of the base build
# context, so no team's strategy ever enters a base layer (COPY layers are additive; a later
# `rm` only whiteouts). Every per-team image is FROM base, so a leak here leaks to everyone.
**/node_modules
.git
runs
cache
*.log
deployer/vendor
deployer/out
dashboard/dist
dashboard/build

# No agent code in the base -- only the shared runtime + lib that bot.ts needs.
example/agents/*
!example/agents/runtime
!example/agents/lib
